## At home

- use **bright lighting**, especially for reading and in the kitchen
- use a magnifier for small print
- reduce glare with blinds and a brimmed hat or sunglasses outdoors
- remove trip hazards and add contrast, such as tape on step edges

## Driving

You must be able to read a car number plate from **20 metres**, with glasses if you need them. If your sight no longer meets this standard, you must stop driving and tell the **DVLA**. Glare at night can be a problem even if you meet the standard.

## Eye tests

Have an eye test at least every 2 years, or more often if advised. NHS sight tests are **free** if you are 60 or over, or have diabetes. See [help with eye care costs](/support/health-costs/eye-care/).

## Support

**RNIB** has a free helpline for anyone worried about their sight.
